{"id":"word:hebrew:H7925","type":"word","title":"שָׁכַם","subtitle":"H7925 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"literally, to load up (on the back of man or beast), i.e. to start early in the morning","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁכַם (H7925) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 65 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁכַם (shâkam) means literally, to load up (on the back of man or beast), i.e. to start early in the morning First listed occurrence: 1Sam 1 19."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁכַם","transliteration":"shâkam","pronunciation":"shaw-kam'","strong":"H7925","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7925","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם","הַשְׁכֵּ֣ם","וַ/יַּשְׁכִּ֣ימוּ","וַ/יַּשְׁכִּ֣מוּ","הַשְׁכֵּ֥ם"],"morphs":[["HC/Vhw3ms",20],["HC/Vhw3mp",16],["HVha",13],["HVhv2ms",3],["HC/Vhq2mp",2],["HVhrmsa",2],["HVhrmpc",2],["HC/Vhq3ms",1],["HC/Vhp2mp",1],["HC/Vha",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"literally, to load up (on the back of man or beast), i.e. to start early in the morning","usage":"(arise, be up, get (oneself) up, rise up) early (betimes), morning.","full":"H7925. shakam [ שָׁכַם ] verb Hiph`il denominative start, rise, early (properly load backs of beasts for day's journey); — Perfect 3masculine singular consecutive וְהִשְׁכִּים 2Sam 15:2 ; Job 1:5 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular וַיַּשְׁכֵּם Gen 19:27 +, 2 masculine singular תְּשְׁכִּים Judg 9:33 , etc.; Imperative הַשְׁכֵּם Exod 8:16 +; Infinitive absolute הַשְׁכֵּם Jer 7:25 +, כֵּים - 44:4 ; Prov 27:14 , erroneous אַשְׁכֵּים Jer 25:3 (Ges § 53 K); Participle מַשְׁכִּים Hosea 6:4 +, etc., — rise early, make an early start , of journey (Hexateuch only J E); לְדַרְכְּכֶם Judg 19:9 (+ מָחָר ), compare Cant 7:13; + verb of going Gen 19:2 (J), standing 2Sam 15:2 (compare Dr), encamping Judg 7:1 , etc.; + infinitive 1Sam 15:12 (compare Dr), 29:11 ; 2Kin 6:15 ( לָקוּם ), קוּם מַשְׁכִּימֵי Psa 127:3 (opposed to שֶׁבֶת מְאַחֲרֵי ); usually with בַּבֹּקֶר Gen 19:27 (J; אֶלהַֿמָּקוֺם ), 1Sam 29:10 (twice in verse) + 27 t., + (hyperbole) יִרְדֹּ֑פוּ בַבּ ׳מַשְׁכִּימֵי שֵׁכָר Isa 5:11 (|| בֵנֶּשֶׁף מְאַחֲרֵי ); with מִמָּחֳרָת Exod 32:6 (E), Judg 6:28 3 t.; with הַשַּׁחַר בַּעֲלוֺת Josh 6:15 (J), 1 Samuel 19:26; וַיֵּצְאוּ וַיַּשְׁכִּימוּ וַיְמַהֲרוּ 8:14 (J) they made a quick and early start; and went out ; Infinitive absolute (Ges § 113s ) as adverb ׳הַשׁ וְהַעֲרֵב 1Sam 17:16 at early morning and at evening ; especially of ׳י , in Jeremiah: וְדַבֵּר ׳הַשׁ = speaking early and often Jer 7:13 ; 35:14 and (of Jeremiah) 25:3 , compare 11:7 ; 32:33 ; often ׳הַשׁ וְשָׁלוֺחַ = sending early and often 7:25 ; 24:4 ; 26:5 ; 29:19 ; 35:14 ; 44:4 , also 2Chr 36:15 ; so verb finite הִשְׁחִיתוּ הִשְׁכִּימוּ , Zeph 3:7 = with eagerness they corrupted (Ges § 120g ); participle מַשְׁ ׳כַּטַּל הֹלֵךְ Hosea 6:4 like the dew departing early , 13:3 (Ges ib .). — 1Sam 9:26 read וַיִּשְׁכַּב , see שׁכב","rootNote":"a primitive root; properly, to incline (the shoulder to a burden); but used only as denominative from 7926 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 1 19","keyReferences":["1Sam 1 19","1Sam 5 3","1Sam 5 4","1Sam 9 26","1Sam 15 12","1Sam 17 16","1Sam 17 20","1Sam 29 10"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":65,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 1 19","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּשְׁכִּ֣מוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 5 3","book":"1Sam","chapter":5,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּשְׁכִּ֤מוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 5 4","book":"1Sam","chapter":5,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּשְׁכִּ֣מוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 9 26","book":"1Sam","chapter":9,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWo